        <Options>
            <Main applyHouseholdOperatingConditions="false" applyReducedOperatingConditions="false" atypicalElectricalLoads="false" waterConservation="false" referenceHouse="false">
                <Vermiculite code="1">
                    <English>Unknown</English>
                    <French>Inconnu</French>
                </Vermiculite>
            </Main>
            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>Air Leakage Areas:



Crawlspace Door



Crawlspace header along front of the house. Vapor barrier has let go in a few places and should be sealed up and fixed properly. 



Back window beside the back door.</airSeal>
                <mainWalls>Add R-15 Type 2 EPS Insulation to the exterior of the home.



Please refer to Artic Energy Alliance for rebates on insulation upgrades and the criteria for these products.</mainWalls>
                <windows>Upgrade windows to ENERGY STAR® Zone 3 rated.



Back window beside the back door should be replaced.



Please refer to Artic Energy Alliance for rebates on windows/doors and the criteria for these products.

</windows>
                <VentilationSystem>The home is quite air tight and should be properly ventilated with a HRV or ERV. A mechanical ventilation system such as an HRV/ERV should be installed to allow the home to be properly ventilated. Not installing a system after air sealing can lead to issues with mold and mildew.



The HRV/ERV will recover heated exhaust air via a heat exchanger and preheat supply air with the extracted heat, making the units very efficient. Make sure the unit is ENERGY STAR® rated and HVI certified.



HRV = Heat Recovery Ventilator

ERV = Enthalpy Recovery Ventilator



ERV also can control indoor humidity levels as well.



Please refer to Artic Energy Alliance for rebates on ventilation systems and the criteria for these products.

</VentilationSystem>
                <HotWaterSystem>The hot water tank is olny 5 years old so is not ready to be replaced yet. When you do replace it, you should install an condensing instananeous on-demand ENERGY STAR®  hot water heater. Make sure the Energy Factor (EF) is 0.92 or higher.



Please refer to Artic Energy Alliance for rebates on DHW systems and the criteria for these products.</HotWaterSystem>
                <HeatingSystem>Install a digital or smart thermostat to help reduce gas consumption.



Upgrade furnace to an ENERGY STAR® condensing gas furnace with a 95% AFUE. Make sure the furnace is equipped with an energy efficient ECM Motor. 



This system will have direct supply/exhaust which will eliminate the need for the fresh supply air duct in thecrawlspace. This will decrease the amount of gas burned during the heating season and will reduce cold air entering the home. 



Only cut off the supply for combustion air if both heating and hot water are direct vented/condensing.



Please refer to Artic Energy Alliance for rebates on heating systems and the criteria for these products.</HeatingSystem>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
